    "body": "## Summary\n\nCloses ADR-037 by flipping status to Implemented, adding an Implementation section that records the **partial visible delta** honestly, and appending a Post-ADR-037 note to ADR-026 (var-inside-calc fix + test transition). **Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The partial delta, honestly measured\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search icon `width` | 2 | **20** ✓ |\n| Search icon `height` | 0 | **0** ✗ |\n\nWidth grew correctly via calc(). Height stayed at 0 because `layout_element` doesn't apply `height` from ComputedStyle to non-`<img>` boxes — a **pre-existing gap unrelated to calc**. Deferred to ADR-040 (box model completion).\n\n## What ADR-037 delivered\n\n### `calc()` / `min()` / `max()` / `clamp()` (~280 lines)\n\n- Standard precedence (`* /` before `+ -`)\n- Nested parens + nested math functions\n- Unary negation\n- Mixed-unit arithmetic (`2em + 8px`, `100% - 20px`, `1rem + 4px`) via convert-to-px-at-parse-time\n- Units: px/em/rem/%/pt (vh/vw deferred)\n\n### `var()` inside calc + composite values (~50 lines)\n\n`resolve_var_whole` extended from whole-value-only to **scan-and-splice any embedded `var()` occurrence**. Recursive.\n\nFixes ADR-026's deferred limitation. Required for `calc(var(--font-size-medium,1rem) + 4px)` — the exact Wikipedia search-icon case.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 431 / 1765\n- After: **456 / 1792** (+25 / +27)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n- CI green (PR + post-merge on #192)\n\nNew `tests/test_calc.cpp`:\n- 20 `[calc]` tests: all operators, precedence, nesting, mixed units, min/max/clamp\n- 5 `[var][adr-037]` tests: var-inside-calc, composite values\n\n## The test-transition record\n\nOne existing test documented ADR-026's deferred behavior:\n\n```cpp\nTEST_CASE(\"var(): partial-value declaration left unchanged (deferred)\") {\n    CHECK(decl.value == \"1px solid var(--border-color, #ccc)\");\n}\n```\n\nADR-037 resolves it. Test renamed to \"...resolved (ADR-037)\" with updated assertion and comment documenting the transition — **same pattern as ADR-029's \"display_of unknown value\" test**. The deferred contract is now delivered; the test name records the shift.\n\n## What ADR-026 still owns\n\n- Whole-value `var()` resolution (fast path)\n- `:root` custom property registration\n- Cascade's `resolve_var_whole` call site\n\n## What ADR-037 added to ADR-026\n\n- Scan-and-splice for embedded `var()` anywhere\n- Recursive resolution\n- Compatibility with all math functions\n\n## What's next\n\nThe arc's pivot is now reflected in the work itself: **spec-driven feature roadmap** (calc/min/max/clamp, then ADR-038 structural pseudos, ADR-039 pseudo-elements + content, ADR-040 box model). Wikipedia remains the validation page, but the ADR menu comes from the CSS spec, not from what happens to break.\n\nRefs #191 #192\n",
